  v_submit["queueRequestDevice returns <br/>-ENOENT if the stream <br/>buffer is missing and <br/>returns 0 if both control <br/>processing and buffer <br/>submission succeed."]
  v_controls["processControls does not <br/>check individual <br/>processControl returns; it <br/>passes the constructed list <br/>to setControls. An empty <br/>list can also return 0, so <br/>0 does not prove that all <br/>requested controls were <br/>applied."]
  v_queue["queueBuffer performs <br/>VIDIOC#95;QBUF. A missing <br/>cache#95; logs Fatal, so it <br/>must not be generalized as <br/>a normal negative return."]
  v_queued["queuedBuffers#95; records <br/>buffers by index after QBUF <br/>succeeds."]
  v_cancel["cancelRequest cancels and <br/>completes the request and <br/>follows the same rules as <br/>completeRequest."]
  v_available["bufferAvailable handles a <br/>separate device completion <br/>event. If DQBUF fails or an <br/>unexpected buffer is <br/>returned, it returns <br/>without a bufferReady <br/>notification."]
  v_ready["imageBufferReady records <br/>the buffer timestamp in the <br/>request, then completes the <br/>buffer and the request in <br/>that order."]
  v_complete["The pipeline handler must <br/>explicitly complete the <br/>request on the <br/>CameraManager thread and <br/>must not access it after <br/>completeRequest returns. It <br/>may call completeRequest on <br/>complete requests without <br/>an ordering constraint, and <br/>requests are returned to <br/>the application in <br/>submission order."]
